<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"><title>Chinese 3 · Paper A · Learner paper · 繁體</title><base href="/api/v1/course-tests/chinese-3/a/file/"><link rel="stylesheet" href="paper.css"></head><body><main><header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">HSKKit · Chinese 3 Course Review · Original Paper A</p><h1>Learner paper · 繁體</h1><p>40 objective questions + 4 writing/speaking tasks · 90-minute section budget.</p><p class="note">Reference materials. Open the workspace for section clocks, local answer saving and recording. Writing and speaking need self-review or your own teacher; no automatic grade.</p><nav class="links"><a href="index.html">Overview</a><a href="student.html">Learner paper</a><a href="student-traditional.html">繁體試卷</a><a href="teacher.html">Answers &amp; scripts</a><a href="listening.html">Listen to Chinese 3 A</a><a href="student.pdf">Learner PDF</a><a href="student-traditional.pdf">繁體 PDF</a><a href="teacher.pdf">Answer PDF</a></nav></header><nav class="links"><a href="#listening">Listening</a><a href="#reading">Reading</a><a href="#writing">Writing</a><a href="#speaking">Speaking</a></nav><h2 class="section-title" id="listening">Listening · 25 minutes</h2><h3>L1 · Questions 1–5</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-1.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L1a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 1</p><p class="gloss">志願活動: volunteer activity</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q1"><h3>1. When did the speaker first help at this school activity?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 上學期剛開學時</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 上學期結束時</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 這學期放假以後</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L1b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 2, 3 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">介紹板: display board</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q2"><h3>2. What had the man expected before his first introduction?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 新同學會先動手做東西</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 新同學都會帶材料來</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 新同學會聽完長介紹</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q3"><h3>3. Why did the second introduction attract more participants?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 把原來的介紹講得更長</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 不再回答新同學的問題</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先讓大家體驗自己能做什麼</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L1c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 4, 5 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">羣消息: group-chat messages</p><p class="gloss">分工: division of tasks</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q4"><h3>4. What need does the woman state?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每天八點以前完成所有作業</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 完全不參加小組討論</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 九點以後不再看羣消息</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q5"><h3>5. What is the likely purpose of the man’s proposal?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 讓大家以後只用電話交流</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 減少一直等消息的負擔，同時保留合作</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 讓不及時回覆的人退出小組</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L2 · Questions 6–10</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-2.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L2a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 6</p><p class="gloss">報名: sign up</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q6"><h3>6. What will the speaker do first to prepare for the future activity?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 這個月馬上報名參加</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 請弟弟替自己講故事</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 每週讀故事並試着複述</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L2b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 7, 8 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">校園廣播: school radio</p><p class="gloss">攝影: photography</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q7"><h3>7. What preparation is required for Activity A?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 星期五前交自己寫的介紹</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 週日下午自己帶相機</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先買一臺新的相機</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q8"><h3>8. Which next step fits the man’s situation?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 直接認定自己已報上甲活動</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 改去只在週日下午開的乙活動</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 修改介紹後確認甲活動是否有名額</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L2c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 9, 10 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">錄音: record audio</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q9"><h3>9. Who is responsible for finding the information?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 陳林</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 蘇安</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 最後整理的人</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q10"><h3>10. What sequence have they finally agreed on?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 週二資料，週四錄音，週五整理後交</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 週三先錄音，再等週四的資料</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 週五交完以後再整理</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L3 · Questions 11–15</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-3.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L3a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 11</p><p class="gloss">採訪: interview</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q11"><h3>11. What is the main purpose of this programme?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 公佈下一次比賽的獲獎名單</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 介紹同學從經歷中改變做法的故事</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 教授參加比賽必須使用的方法</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L3b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 12, 13 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">封面: cover</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q12"><h3>12. How does Xiaoyu’s view of the notebook change?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 從只看新舊，變爲注意裏面記錄的經歷</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 從想買新本子，變爲以後都不用新本子</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 從喜歡畫畫，變爲只願意寫字</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q13"><h3>13. Which attitude is best supported by the ending?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 按具體用途和記憶決定去留</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 舊東西越多就一定越好</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只要封面漂亮就應該留下</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L3c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 14, 15 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">修補: mend</p><p class="gloss">提手: handle</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q14"><h3>14. What must participants do before the morning activity?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 先交修補工具的錢</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 把要修的布袋洗乾淨</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先把所有舊書整理完</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q15"><h3>15. Which plan fits the man’s availability and goal?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 下午參加舊書整理</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 下午纔開始修補布袋</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 上午參加布袋修補</div></div></article></div></section><h3>L4 · Questions 16–20</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/listening-group-4.mp3"></audio><p class="note">6:15 group track: 1 + 2 + 2 questions across three sources; each source plays twice, with answering pauses.</p><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L4a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 16</p><p class="gloss">堆放: pile up</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q16"><h3>16. What is the revised collection time?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 週六上午九點</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 週五下午九點</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 週六下午原定時間</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L4b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 17, 18 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">匆忙: hurried</p><p class="gloss">從容: unhurried</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q17"><h3>17. What change does Xiaoning try this month?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 一寫完作業就立刻出門</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 睡前半小時不用手機</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 每天早上多花半小時找東西</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q18"><h3>18. What explains her reported change in the morning?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 兩週以後不再需要準備書包</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 晚上先放好書包，早上少了找東西</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 她保證每天都完全做到計劃</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-L4c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 19, 20 · Shared material</p><p class="gloss">長跑: distance running</p><p class="gloss">悶着: keep feelings to oneself</p><p class="gloss">名次: placing in a competition</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q19"><h3>19. Which suggestion fits the woman’s present circumstances?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每天練習一小時再決定是否活動</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 約朋友走十分鐘，不以比賽爲目標</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 等到有完整比賽時間纔開始活動</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q20"><h3>20. What does the man’s reflection suggest he now values?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 共同堅持的過程，不只看名次</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只有得到獎纔算值得參加</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 不再願意和朋友一起活動</div></div></article></div></section><h2 class="section-title" id="reading">Reading · 30 minutes</h2><h3>R1 · Questions 21–25</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R1a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 21</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">上學期第一個星期五，學校請我們幫助新同學。我原來以爲自己要站在門口講話，到了才知道，老師讓我陪兩位同學找實驗教室。我先看了樓層圖，再帶他們上樓。那天下午我說的話不多，卻一直在認真聽他們的問題。回家後，我把這次第一次幫助別人的經歷寫進了日記。</p></div><p class="gloss">實驗教室: science classroom</p><p class="gloss">樓層圖: floor plan</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q21"><h3>21. When did the writer help the new students?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 上學期最後一個星期五</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 上學期第一個星期五</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 本學期第一天</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R1b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 22, 23 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">我參加校刊小組以前，總以爲採訪就是提前寫好問題，再請對方一個個回答。第一次採訪門口的保安叔叔時，我把問題問完就準備離開。他笑着問，我要不要聽聽他最難忘的一天。我這才放下本子，認真聽他講有一次怎樣幫助迷路的新生。<br>回到小組，我沒有按原來的問題順序寫文章，而是先寫那一天發生的事，再補上人物介紹。老師說，讀者因此更容易瞭解他的工作。我發現，準備問題當然有用，但願意聽對方想講的事情也很重要。下次採訪，我還會準備問題，卻不會只盯着自己的本子。</p></div><p class="gloss">校刊: school magazine</p><p class="gloss">保安: security guard</p><p class="gloss">新生: new student</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q22"><h3>22. What did the writer originally expect an interview to be?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 完全不用提前準備任何問題</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 由被採訪的人替自己寫文章</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 按事先寫好的問題逐個問答</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q23"><h3>23. Why did the writer change the article’s organization?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因爲老師要求刪除所有人物介紹</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 因爲原來沒有準備任何採訪問題</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先呈現具體經歷，更便於讀者理解人物工作</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R1c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 24, 25 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小組通知：我們要在週四放學前交一份校園生活介紹。週二請每個人提出一個主題，週三中午一起確定內容。資料可以從校園觀察中獲得，不要求採訪校外的人。每個人都要負責一小部分，不能只由一位同學完成。<br>小梅回覆：我週三中午要參加合唱練習，不能開會。我願意整理食堂排隊的觀察，週二晚上就把筆記發給大家。請你們先討論；如果主題合適，再告訴我需要補什麼。我週四午休還能修改，但放學後不能留下來。</p></div><p class="gloss">合唱: choir</p><p class="gloss">排隊: queue</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q24"><h3>24. By when must the group submit its introduction?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 週三中午開會前</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 週四放學前</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 週四放學以後</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q25"><h3>25. What is a reasonable next action for the other members?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 等週四放學後再讓她開始找資料</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 週三討論她的筆記，儘早反饋供她週四午休修改</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 因爲她不能開會，就認定她不能參與</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R2 · Questions 26–30</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R2a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 26</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">林安想在下學期參加學校的故事分享小組。她喜歡讀書，卻發現自己講故事時容易漏掉中間的經過。她給這個月定了一個小目標：每週讀完一篇短故事，寫下三個先後發生的動作，再試着不看書講給同伴聽。她暫時沒有報名，準備月末聽聽同伴的意見，再決定是否參加。</p></div><p class="gloss">漏掉: leave out</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q26"><h3>26. What is Lin’an’s preparation plan for this month?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 每週讀故事，記動作順序，再試着複述</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 先報名，再請別人代替自己讀書</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只記故事結尾，不再練習講述</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R2b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 27, 28 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">下月學校開放兩種體驗活動。甲是星期六上午的講解練習，參加者先觀察一處校園空間，再在週五前交一份簡短介紹。老師提供圖片，不需要自己買設備。乙是星期日下午的影像記錄，參加者須帶能夠拍攝的設備，並提前學習一種剪輯工具。兩個活動都可以幫助同學整理信息，但練習方式不同。<br>小禾希望以後能把複雜事情講得更清楚。她只有星期六上午有空，已經記下了圖書角的使用情況，卻還沒有整理成介紹。她不想爲了這次活動購買設備。她準備先看清要求，再確認是否還有位置，不會僅因時間合適就當作報名成功。</p></div><p class="gloss">剪輯: video editing</p><p class="gloss">設備: equipment</p><p class="gloss">圖書角: classroom reading corner</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q27"><h3>27. Which difference between the activities is stated?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 甲練習講解並提供圖片，乙要帶拍攝設備</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 甲要求購買設備，乙完全不需要準備</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 甲乙都只在星期日下午進行</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q28"><h3>28. Which action best matches Xiaohe’s goal and constraints?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 購買新設備後報名乙，不考慮週日時間</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 把觀察整理成介紹，再詢問甲的名額</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 僅憑甲的時間合適就停止準備</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R2c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 29, 30 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">活動公告：讀書社本週要製作一張共同推薦單。每人選擇一個校園生活話題，寫出自己的看法和一個具體例子。週三晚上八點前發給負責人，週四中午討論，再於放學前定稿。推薦單不要求所有人意見相同，但每一項都要說明理由。<br>周寧的回覆：我想談午休時怎樣使用圖書角。我認爲應該留出安靜讀書的地方，因爲上次大家同時討論時，有同學沒法專心。我週四中午有事，不過週三晚上七點能發來內容，也願意在討論前補充一個例子。請把討論後的修改意見發給我，我當天放學前還有時間調整。</p></div><p class="gloss">推薦單: recommendation list</p><p class="gloss">定稿: finalize</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q29"><h3>29. What reason does Zhou Ning give for a quiet reading space?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 負責人要求所有人意見一樣</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 圖書角週四中午將不開放</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 討論聲曾影響同學專心讀書</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q30"><h3>30. Does Zhou Ning’s proposed contribution fit the stated process?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 可以，七點先交看法和例子，再按討論意見修改</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 不可以，因爲公告禁止缺席會議的人交內容</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 可以，但必須等週四討論結束才第一次交內容</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R3 · Questions 31–35</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R3a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 31</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">校園廣播本週開設“試過以後”小欄目，不介紹比賽成績，而請同學講一次自己改變辦法的經歷。第一期有人談怎樣從只讀書名改成先翻目錄，也有人談怎樣把難記的路線畫出來。節目最後會請聽衆選擇一種願意嘗試的辦法，並寫下一週後的感受。欄目並不保證每種辦法都適合每個人。</p></div><p class="gloss">欄目: programme segment</p><p class="gloss">目錄: table of contents</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q31"><h3>31. What is the main idea of this programme introduction?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 分享改變做法的經歷，並鼓勵有選擇地嘗試</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 按比賽成績給全校同學排出名次</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 保證聽衆使用同一種辦法都能成功</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R3b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 32, 33 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">短故事《不一樣的禮物》中，小嵐想給朋友做一本相冊。她起初只找顏色漂亮的紙，覺得好看就夠了。後來她看到朋友保留的一張模糊照片：那是兩人第一次一起完成小組任務時拍的。照片並不清楚，朋友卻把它放在書桌上。<br>小嵐於是把那張照片放在相冊第一頁，旁邊寫下當時大家怎樣互相幫忙。其他頁面仍然用了她喜歡的彩紙，但每頁都多了一段小記。朋友說，自己最喜歡的是那些一起經歷過的事。故事結尾，朋友把相冊放在常看的書架上，翻到第一頁，笑着又說起那天的事。小嵐看着旁邊還沒用完的彩紙，決定留着做下一份禮物。</p></div><p class="gloss">相冊: photo album</p><p class="gloss">模糊: blurred</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q32"><h3>32. Why does Xiaolan put the unclear photo on the first page?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因爲朋友只喜歡看不清楚的照片</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 它記錄了兩人共同完成任務的經歷</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 因爲她決定整本相冊不再用彩紙</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q33"><h3>33. Which interpretation best fits the ending?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 外觀之外，共同經歷也能讓禮物有意義</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 所有好看的禮物都沒有價值</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只有模糊照片才值得保存</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R3c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 34, 35 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">學校準備舉行一次舊物再用活動。修補區只接收已經清洗的布袋，工具由老師提供，參加者須先說明哪裏需要修補。分享區接收內容完整、適合同齡人閱讀的舊書，不收缺頁的練習冊。兩個區域都在週六上午開放，大家可以按自己的需要選擇，不必每個區域都去。<br>小齊想讓破了一個小口的布袋繼續使用，家裏的幾本書也想帶來。她週六只有一個小時，因此決定先把袋子洗好，再檢查書頁。如果書適合分享，就在修袋前先送到分享區；如果書有缺頁，就暫時留下處理，而不是把它交給別人。她最想完成的仍是修好布袋。</p></div><p class="gloss">缺頁: missing pages</p><p class="gloss">同齡人: people of the same age</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q34"><h3>34. What does the sharing area refuse?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 缺頁的練習冊</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 內容完整且適合同齡人的舊書</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 所有已經讀過的書</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q35"><h3>35. Which plan meets Xiaoqi’s goal and the event’s rules?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 不檢查書頁，把有缺頁的書先送走</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 爲了每區都參加，放棄自己最想修好的布袋</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 先洗袋查書，再按書的狀況決定是否分享並修袋</div></div></article></div></section><h3>R4 · Questions 36–40</h3><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R4a"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 36</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">“少用一次性杯子”活動只針對本週的讀書分享會。學校鼓勵同學帶自己的杯子，但忘帶的人可以借用會場清洗好的杯子，結束後放回指定位置。通知提醒，活動不是要求大家馬上扔掉家裏所有舊杯子，也不限制正常喝水。負責人希望先從一次活動開始，看看怎樣做更方便。</p></div><p class="gloss">一次性: single-use</p><p class="gloss">指定: designated</p><div class="single-question"><article class="question" id="q36"><h3>36. Which statement correctly describes the initiative’s scope?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 要求全校立刻扔掉所有舊杯子</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 先在本週分享會試行，忘帶杯子可以借</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 本週沒有自帶杯子的人都不能喝水</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R4b"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 37, 38 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小青的兩週記錄：以前我總在睡前才找第二天要用的東西，有時一邊找一邊看手機，早上又要確認一次。這兩週我試着喫完晚飯就把書包整理好，睡前留十分鐘聽輕鬆的音樂。不是每天都按計劃做到，不過我把做到和沒做到的日子都記了下來。<br>第二週末，我發現自己早上少找了幾次作業本，出門時也沒有那麼急。我願意再試兩週，看看遇到作業多的時候還能不能堅持。朋友建議我直接說“這個辦法人人都該用”，我沒有這樣寫：這些只是我的記錄，也可能有別的原因影響那幾天的感受。我想先繼續觀察，再決定怎樣調整。</p></div><p class="gloss">確認: check/confirm</p><p class="gloss">觀察: observe</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q37"><h3>37. What change does Xiaoqing explicitly report?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 從此每天都絕不會再着急</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 已經證明這個辦法適合所有人</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 早上找作業本的次數少了幾次</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q38"><h3>38. Why does she decide to keep observing?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 因爲兩週裏她從來沒有一次做到計劃</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 因爲她已經確定所有變化只由音樂造成</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 已有一些變化，但還要看忙碌時是否可堅持</div></div></article></div></section><section class="material-block" data-material="C3A-R4c"><p class="eyebrow">Questions 39, 40 · Shared material</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">去年參加校園尋路活動時，我一心想讓小組最快到達。走錯一次後，我一直埋怨自己，差點不想繼續。隊友沒有催我，反而請我畫下剛纔經過的路口。我們雖然沒拿到名次，卻一起找到了終點。我後來最常想起的，是大家願意停下來重新商量的那一刻。<br>最近同學邀請我參加新的小組活動。我每週只有兩次放學後的短時間，不可能天天準備。我決定先說明這個限制，問能否負責一小段路線記錄。如果大家同意，我就按時完成這部分，再聽取反饋。這一次，我把給小組的第一條消息改了三遍，最後寫的是自己能完成什麼、希望得到什麼反饋，而不是先問有沒有機會拿第一。</p></div><p class="gloss">埋怨: blame/complain about</p><p class="gloss">反饋: feedback</p><div class="paired-questions"><article class="question" id="q39"><h3>39. Which current adjustment is supported by the past experience and present limits?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 承諾每天都能準備，避免提到時間限制</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 說明可用時間，協商一項能完成的路線記錄任務</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 只有保證小組第一名才願意參加</div></div></article><article class="question" id="q40"><h3>40. What can reasonably be inferred about the writer’s changed view?</h3><div class="options"><div class="option"><b>A.</b> 只要出錯，以後就不該參加小組活動</div><div class="option"><b>B.</b> 只要大家一起參加，就不必完成自己的工作</div><div class="option"><b>C.</b> 更重視可完成的合作過程，而不只看名次</div></div></article></div></section><h2 class="section-title" id="writing">Writing · 25 minutes</h2><p>W1 and W2 share 25 minutes. Use paper or your own editor; this review page does not save answers.</p><section class="box" id="W1"><p class="eyebrow">writing · W1</p><h2>Reply to a club disagreement</h2><p>Reply to Lin in Chinese. Answer whether you can join Wednesday’s discussion and whether you prefer interviews or a display. Explain your preference. Address the new restriction with a feasible alternative, and ask one relevant clarification or confirmation. You may invent personal details. About 60-90 Chinese characters is guidance, not a minimum.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">小禾：我們要介紹學校的舊物再用活動。你週三午休能來討論嗎？你更想採訪同學，還是做圖片展示？現在老師說放學後不能再進教室，大家原來約好的時間不行了。請你想個辦法，也告訴我還有什麼需要確認。<br>小林</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Answer whether you can join Wednesday lunchtime.</li><li>Choose interviews, a display or another relevant format.</li><li>Give a reason for your preference.</li><li>Offer a feasible way to work without after-school access.</li><li>Ask one relevant clarification or confirmation.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><section class="box" id="W2"><p class="eyebrow">writing · W2</p><h2>When an activity turned out differently</h2><p>Using the fictional activity card, write connected Chinese paragraphs for a classmate about an experience that changed your view. Include its time and context, at least two actions in sequence, the contrast between expectation and outcome, a reason or feeling, and one reflection or next step. You may add plausible details consistent with the card. About 140-180 Chinese characters is guidance, not a minimum.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">虛構活動卡<br>時間：上個月一個週六上午<br>地點：學校舊物再用活動<br>原先期待：擔心不會修東西，覺得只能旁觀<br>經過：先聽老師介紹；幫助整理布袋；和同學一起修好鬆開的提手<br>結果：雖然不快，仍然幫助了別人<br>感受和下一步：自行選擇，可表達仍有困難，但須與材料一致</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Establish last month’s Saturday morning and the school reuse activity.</li><li>Describe one action from the card.</li><li>Describe a second action in a consistent sequence.</li><li>Contrast the original expectation with what happened.</li><li>Explain a feeling or a reason.</li><li>State a specific reflection or next step.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><h2 class="section-title" id="speaking">Speaking · 10 minutes</h2><section class="box" id="S1"><p class="eyebrow">speaking · S1</p><h2>Discuss a goal and a change of plan</h2><p>Respond in Chinese to four fixed prompts from a classmate about a school project. Each file already contains two plays. Play it once, then allow 15 seconds to prepare and up to 30 seconds to respond. Link your opinion, an experience, an alternative and a next step. You may invent details. All four responses form one task /8; this is not an adaptive conversation.</p><p>You and a classmate are preparing a short introduction for a school activity. Personal experience may be fictional.</p><ul class="checklist"><li>State an opinion or need.</li><li>Use an experience to explain a reason.</li><li>Respond to a new condition with a feasible alternative.</li><li>Explain a final choice and next step.</li></ul><h3>S1-1</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-1.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-2</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-2.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-3</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-3.mp3"></audio><h3>S1-4</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/audio/s1-4.mp3"></audio><p class="note">Each file already plays the prompt twice. Play it once; then prepare for 15 seconds and respond for up to 30 seconds. Four responses are one /8 task.</p><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section><section class="box" id="S2"><p class="eyebrow">speaking · S2</p><h2>Recommend a school action</h2><p>Recommend one of the two supplied plans to your class. Compare the plans, support your recommendation with two details from the card, identify one limitation, and give a practical next step. Either choice can receive full credit if its constraints are addressed. You have 60 seconds to prepare and up to 120 seconds to speak. Instructions are on screen, not a separate audio prompt.</p><div class="source"><p class="cn">班級情況：20人，週六上午有空，希望多數同學能參與；材料總預算50元。<br>甲：舊書分享，週六9:00–11:00，免費，每人帶一本內容完整的書；圖書角同時最多10人，可分批；需要2位同學整理推薦單。<br>乙：布袋修補，週六9:30–11:30，老師提供工具和補布，共需材料費30元；同時最多12人，本週只有這一場；學習者須帶洗淨的布袋。<br>可以推薦任一方案，但要說明怎樣處理人數、準備或其他限制。</p></div><ul class="checklist"><li>Compare a relevant feature of both plans.</li><li>Make a clear recommendation.</li><li>Give a first supporting detail from the card.</li><li>Give a different second supporting detail.</li><li>Identify a limitation of the recommended plan.</li><li>Propose a next step that addresses it.</li></ul><p class="badge">Manual /8 · no automatic grade</p></section></main></body></html>